> XDrip+. It seems that for small changes arrow is always pointing from left to right ->, in Xdrip there is arrow that is just little slanted, I think in AAPS that one doesn't exists...

What I see in the code, the `FortyFiveUp` arrow should be shown with delta +7 in 5 minutes.
In that case, the `slope_by_minute` should result in 1.4.
```
if (slope_by_minute <= (-3.5)) {
    arrow = "DoubleDown";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (-2)) {
    arrow = "SingleDown";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (-1)) {
    arrow = "FortyFiveDown";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (1)) {
    arrow = "Flat";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (2)) {
    arrow = "FortyFiveUp";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (3.5)) {
    arrow = "SingleUp";
} else if (slope_by_minute <= (40)) {
    arrow = "DoubleUp";
}
```
